Phasmid: CSS family names (Windows profiles)

What:     A windows profile with a Windows font store resolves CSS family
          names as DirectWrite does. Faces are named by their
          weight-stretch-style family (name ID 21, else the typographic
          family plus its subfamily's non-style words, else the legacy family
          with its style words moved into the style; a variable font's named
          instance by its STAT-derived family) and chosen as
          GetFirstMatchingFont chooses them. A name with no such family is
          retried once as "<family> <weight or stretch word>". Linux profiles
          and runs without a store are unchanged.
Why:      fontconfig names faces by their legacy families, so names Windows
          resolves were missing (Franklin Gothic, Sitka Small), names it
          rejects resolved (Arial Rounded MT Bold), and some names drew a
          different face.
Profile:  os.family, fonts.families
Hooks:    components/services/font/font_service_app.cc
          FontServiceApp::MatchFamilyName;
          third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/skia/font_cache_skia.cc
          FontCache::CreateFontPlatformData
Contexts: main, same- and cross-origin iframe, worker, shared worker, service
          worker, OffscreenCanvas in workers; headless and headful.
Guard:    tests/guards/fonts/windows_family_names.py

